- Dreative visual smoke passes at desktop, 390px, 320px and 390px reduced motion.
- Filtering, sold-out sizes, adding Pleated Trouser/L, bag pricing, free delivery and Escape-close were exercised.
- Normal motion changes the pixel field; reduced motion remains static.
- No tested console errors or document overflow.

Material deviations:

- The rail uses native horizontal snap and arrows instead of hijacking vertical-wheel scrolling.
- The mobile filter is no longer sticky because it visibly covered product content during reduced-motion testing.

Delivery remains formally incomplete: `dreative finalize` cannot print `DREATIVE_CHECKS_PASSED` because its `docs-check` rejects the freshly installed Dreative package. `dreative install-skill --check` reports the installation is exact, while `docs-check` reports roughly 50 contradictory missing-contract findings. This is a CLI/package consistency blocker, not an application failure.

No commit was created. Human taste verdict: awaiting user review.
